  "body": {
    "id": "thm:weighted-erasure-spread",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "There exist universal \\(c_0,c_1,c_2\\in(0,1)\\) such that, for every \\(0<\\alpha\\le1/4\\) and every \\((w,q)\\) with \\(\\sum_lq_ls_l^2=1\\) and \\(\\|s\\|_\\infty\\sqrt{x_\\alpha}\\le c_0\\), one has \\([-c_2\\sqrt{x_\\alpha},c_2\\sqrt{x_\\alpha}]\\subseteq\\mathcal T_{\\mathrm{tilt}}\\), and every measurable, possibly externally randomized interval \\(\\Lambda(O,R)\\) obeys\n\\[\n\\inf_{|t|\\le c_2\\sqrt{x_\\alpha}}Q_t\\{T(V)\\in\\Lambda(O,R)\\}\\ge1-\\alpha\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\sup_{|t|\\le c_2\\sqrt{x_\\alpha}}\\mathbb E_{Q_t}\\operatorname{len}\\{\\Lambda(O,R)\\}\n\\ge c_1\\min\\{1,\\sqrt{Sx_\\alpha}\\}.\n\\]",
    "free_symbols": [
      "alpha",
      "x",
      "w",
      "q",
      "s",
      "S",
      "L",
      "l",
      "mathcalTtilt",
      "Lambda",
      "O",
      "R",
      "Q",
      "t",
      "T",
      "V"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:tilted-sign-prior",
      "def:weighted-erasure-law",
      "lem:product-erasure-interval-calculus"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "By \\(s_l=w_l/(q_l\\sqrt S)\\),\n\\[\n \\sum_lq_ls_l^2={1\\over S}\\sum_l{w_l^2\\over q_l}=1.\n\\]\nChoose \\(c_0=c_{\\mathrm e}\\), \\(c_2=c_{\\mathrm p}\\), and \\(c_1=c_{\\mathrm s}\\) from \\(\\mathrm{lem{:}product\\text{-}erasure\\text{-}interval\\text{-}calculus}\\).  Since \\(c_0c_2\\le1\\), \\(|t|\\|s\\|_\\infty\\le1\\) whenever \\(|t|\\le c_2\\sqrt{x_\\alpha}\\); hence this interval is contained in \\(\\mathcal T_{\\mathrm{tilt}}\\) by \\(\\mathrm{def{:}tilted\\text{-}sign\\text{-}prior}\\).  The implication is exactly the first conclusion of the cited proved calculus lemma, under the joint laws in \\(\\mathrm{def{:}weighted\\text{-}erasure\\text{-}law}\\).  Its last conditioning step includes the independent \\(R\\), so no restriction to deterministic intervals is made.",
